    return (
        (
            "Sunlight drives photosynthesis and is essential for plant productivity. "
            "Most fruiting vegetables (tomato, pepper, corn) require 6–8 hours of "
            "direct sunlight daily. Insufficient light weakens plants, reduces "
            "yields, and makes them more vulnerable to fungal diseases due to "
            "slower transpiration and reduced stomatal activity."
        ),
        [
            "Ensure fruiting vegetables receive at least 6 hours of direct sun daily.",
            "Rotate planting locations yearly to prevent shading from permanent structures.",
            "Prune excessive canopy on tree crops to let light penetrate to lower branches.",
            "In hot climates, afternoon shade cloth (30–40 %) can protect sensitive crops.",
            "Leggy, pale growth is a sign of insufficient light; relocate if possible.",
        ],
        ["watering", "soil health", "healthy plants"],
    )


